jo.responsibilities:
Under the direct supervision of the Human Resources Officer, and overall supervision of the Chief of Human Resources, the incumbent is required to perform the following functions:

General

Provides advice and support to managers and staff on Learning & Development matters on performance management processes and tools;
Keeps abreast of developments in various areas of human resources.

Staff development and career support training

Identifies and analyzes staff development and career support needs and designs programmes to meet identified needs, and assists the Unit Chief in the evaluation of training programmes (relevance, impact, etc.); including contributing to the development and delivery of learning programmes,and the development and maintenance of learning materials, guidance notes, communication products and evaluation of pilot projects
Coordinates all arrangements for the centrally organized staff development programmes (including planning, budgeting, implementing, and reporting) and liaises closely with counterparts in OHRM on all training/learning matters;
Organizes and implements the annual training plan for upgrading substantive and technical skills and other career support programmes in consultation with management, line managers and staff; including supporting the delivery of workshops, briefings and learning events aimed at strengthening managerial and interpersonal competencies; acts as focal point for the work of the Learning Coordinators;
Coordinates the management of ESCAP's Learning Centre and provides support in other related work, including supporting learning and awareness activities related to workplace conflict prevention and resolution, as and when necessary; plans, organizes, and coordinates the development and implementation of the following programmes:  language training, IT training, orientation/induction, pre-retirement, mentoring, tests and examinations; performance management, supervisory skills and workplace conflict resolution;
Monitors participation in mandatory learning programmes and ensures systems are in place for new staff to participate in such programmes;
Assists the Unit Chief in the administration of performance management, including reporting on compliance and all related training;
Provides inputs to the preparation of the proposed programme budget for training and development, monitors the use and allocation of the funds and prepares budgetary reports.

Other duties

Participates in human resources projects and innovations to improve processes and client service delivery and the use of automation and digital solutions across HR functions; assists in identifying opportunities to improve HR service delivery through the application of technology, automation and digital tools.
May supervise Human Resources Assistants in the team;
Serve as back-up to staffing/recruitment and staff administration, as and when needed;
Carries out other functions as required.

Under the supervision of the English Press Editor and the Chief of the Section, the incumbent will be responsible for the following duties:

•Drafts summaries, which are issued as press releases and meeting summaries, on the activities and meetings of human rights intergovernmental bodies and treaty bodies in Geneva, including human rights treaty bodies, the Human Rights Council and the Conference on Disarmament;
•Drafts background releases outlining issues to be reviewed by these bodies prior to their sessions, as well as round-up releases summarizing the main decisions adopted;
•Drafts other types of press releases such as highlights of presentations of UN reports, articles on activities of the United Nations Office at Geneva, and credentials;
•Drafts information material such as summaries of press conferences, briefing notes, leaflets, and other information on the activities of the Organization;

•Supports the Press Editor by editing press releases, meeting summaries and other information material;
•Liaises with the secretariats of UN bodies, in particular within OHCHR, and with the Conference on Disarmament in relation with coverage activities;
•Contributes to outreach activities, including preparing and making presentations to students; assisting with the roll-out of communication campaigns; and promoting international UN Days,
•Drafts content for the website and social media, posts it and monitors social media pages;

•Serves as UNIS focal point on AI matters and represents the Service at DGC AI Lab meetings;

• Provides basic technical support and troubleshooting for web content, digital platforms and multimedia products to ensure their effective functioning and publication.
•Assists with other public information tasks as required.

unofficial.duties:
Three main responsibilities:

- Support the ECE's Steering Committee on Trade Capacity and Standards (SCTCS), including organizing its annual session (usually in June) and drafting official documents and reports, preparing for scenario and Chair's notes, liaising with MSs and PMs on official and informal communications;

- Support the annual reporting of the SCTCS Chair to the ECE Executive Committee (EXCOM), including drafting official reports and decisions and preparing for the TPs and slides for the Chair;

- Provide programme management support for the Trade subprogramme, including drafting programme of work and reporting deliverables, as well as liaising with ECE's Programme Management Unit.

jo.responsibilities:
i) Participate in the development of the annual work programme and budget for UN-Habitat:

• Be part if the team that prepares the schedule of work, required tools e.g. guidelines, templates necessary for developing the Annual Programme of Work;

• Participate in the organized dialogues and workshops by Programme Planning and Budget Division to ensure all needed changes in the development of the Annual Programme of Work are cascaded to the relevant staff;

• Support the development of the Programme of Work including reaching out to Suprogrammes and regional Offices to ensure that all their inputs are incorporated into the draft annual work programme;

• Support the collation, review, editing and formatting of the Annual Programme of Work;

• Consolidate and include all inputs from internal and external reviews ensure they are reflected in the updated document;

• Support intergovernmental processes including review of work programme and budget document by the UN-Habitat Executive Board, the Committee on Permanent Representatives; the Advisory Committee on Administrative and Budgetary Questions (ACABQ) and Committee for Programme and Coordination (CPC); including preparation of support documents; Upload the fascicles into the Strategic Management Application in Umoja.

(ii) Participate in monitoring and reporting of the Annual Programme of Work:

• Lead in development of tools required for reporting on the Annual Programme of Work implementation as and when required for review; v • Support managers in reporting on annual work programme and uploading the performance information in UMOJA in relation to implementation of deliverables, update of indicator data, and results achieved at outcome level for Annual Programme of Work;

• Support preparation of the Quarterly reports and annual progress report for Annual Programme of Work implementation, including tools development, data analysis, review of case stories, report design and layout;

(iii)Coordinate the deployment and use of Integrated Planning Monitoring and Reporting system (IPMR) within Corporate Management Division (CMD):

• Coordinate the preparation and submission of a full division wide user mapping of staff members to the 3 IPMR roles;

• Support organization of discussion forums/meetings as may be necessary with Corporate Management Division (CMD) Core Users;

• Coordinate the inputs of Corporate Management Division (CMD) into the overall corporate discussions related to the deployment of IPMR in UN Habitat;

• Participate in discussions with other focal points (from other divisions and regions) in relation to the best approach to take in the deployment of IPMR across the Agency and within Corporate Management Division (CMD) specifically (including delivering of training)

(iv) Participate in coordination of Results based Management activities:

• Be part of the team that develops required RBM training tools and materials and facilitates training RBM for Regional Offices and the Headquarter staff;

• Provide relevant training statistics whenever needed for senior management and donor reviews;

• Ensure efficient and effective training for institutionalization of RBM in UN-Habitat carried out.

Within delegated authority, the Associate Statistician will be responsible for the following duties:

Participates in the collection, evaluation, analysis, compilation and dissemination of  social and gender statistics and data from Member States by selecting methods of data collection, selecting and implementing appropriate methods for validating collected data and processing data for incorporation into statistical database(s);
Assist in capacity development and technical support to countries on social and gender statistics production, and review relevant country practices;
Assist in the development or revision of standards for data and metadata on gender, international migration, time-use and other social statistics, including statistical concepts, definitions and classifications;
Conduct methodological research, analyze, and present information gathered from various data sources on assigned topics;
Prepare draft technical documents for international, intergovernmental and expert group meetings, and assist in drafting relevant technical reports;
Assist in the organization and conduction of seminars, workshops and expert meetings;
Collaborate with general service and professional staff in the section, branch and division;
Maintain close liaison and cooperation with relevant counterparts in national and international institutions, including headquarters, regional commissions, specialized agencies and national governments;
Perform other duties as assigned.

Within delegated authority, the Associate Press Officer will be responsible for the following:

•    Covering meetings of the General Assembly and its Main Committees, the Security Council and other major bodies of the United Nations, as a member of a two-person coverage team that produces a one-shots, 2-3-page news articles format;

•    Covering meetings alone, occasionally, when such single coverage is decided upon by an editor; the selected candidate must be able to take statements from the floor by listening  to speakers and summarizing what is being said while the meeting is in progress;

•    Researching, on the basis of official UN documentation and other sources, background materials to gain familiarity with specific topics or themes related to major meetings or conferences;

•    Reporting accurately and determining levels of substance for expeditious issuance of the coverage;

•    Performing other duties as assigned.

Under the overall supervision of the Secretary of the Fifth Committee and CPC, the Associate Programme Management Officer, Administration will be responsible for the following duties:

• Works with key clients to facilitate the development, implementation and evaluation of the work programme of the Committees, including with the Department of General Assembly and Conference Management and relevant offices on the preparation of documentation for the Committees;

• Analyzes and prepares documents on appointments and elections under the purview of the Fifth Committee, including liaising with the Office of Legal Affairs as required;

• Assists in the preparation of the draft programme of work, status of documentation and the reports of the Committees;

• Reviews the preparation of the notes for the Chair of the Committees and reviewing the Journal summaries and entries; identifies problems and issues to be addressed and recommends corrective actions; liaises with relevant parties; identifies and tracks follow-up actions.

• Contributes to the collection, integration, and analysis of data on selected aspects of programmes. operations and other activities, etc., as well as identification of trends or patterns.

• Supports data-driven planning, progress monitoring, decision-making by contributing to the development of digital reporting tools as well as preparing and updating graphs, charts, tables, and reports and other data visualizations.

• Participates in survey initiatives; assists with design of data collection tools; issues data collection tools, reviews, analyzes and interprets responses, identifies problems/issues and prepares preliminary conclusions.

• Contributes to the preparation of various written outputs, e.g. draft background papers, analytical notes, sections of reports and studies, inputs to publications, etc.

• Prepares substantive summaries of the meetings of the Committees;

• Provides administrative and substantive support to consultative and other meetings, conferences, etc., to include proposing agenda topics, identifying and proposed participants, preparation of background documents and presentations, handling logistics, etc.

• Assists in the activities related to budget performance activities of the Office and preparation of related documents/reports (work programme/RBB framework, programme budget, support account budget, etc.).

• Performs other duties as required, including assisting the Secretary during informal consultations of the Committees.

Within delegated authority, the Associate Travel Officer will be responsible for the following duties:

(a) Travel Business and Systems Support

      i. Travel Business Support

Supports management in monitoring operational performance, including through the use of business intelligence reporting tools;
Liaises with process experts across business and functional areas to define, harmonize and align cross-functional business processes.
      ii. Systems Support

Defines business requirements and establishes priorities for system enhancements;
Ensures that system enhancements are developed in accordance with approved specifications;
Coordinates the testing of system enhancements across the global travel community.
(b) Training

Delivers training to Local Process Experts (LPEs) and end users;
Supports and provides advice on the development and revision of training materials;
Develops user aids and guidance documentation for business processes not covered in detail by Umoja training materials.
(c) Production Support

Provides timely responses to functional inquiries from end users and Local Process Experts (LPEs) across the Secretariat;
Provides intensive support to Local Process Experts, as required;
Contributes to the Community of Practice by responding to frequently asked questions and sharing knowledge and best practices.
(d) Continued Implementation of Umoja Travel in the Secretariat

Conducts change impact assessments by comparing current ("as-is") and future ("to-be") processes and analyzing the implications of change, including changes to roles and responsibilities;
Leads data conversion activities, including data collection, cleansing, enrichment and validation, for all required data types (e.g., master and transactional data) across implementation phases, including mock conversions, dress rehearsals and cutover activities;
Leads testing activities, including Product Integration Testing (PIT) and User Verification Testing (UVT), to validate Umoja travel solutions;
Conducts user access mapping and workflow design, taking into account delegation of authority, departmental responsibilities, user roles and functional skill requirements.

Within delegated authority, the Associate Finance & Budget Officer will be responsible for the following duties:

Programme plan:

• Ensures day-to-day administration of assigned commercial insurance programmes covering UN offices, peace-keeping missions, agencies, and programmes at Headquarters and overseas;

• Reviews, analyses and finalizes the preparation of the programme plan and its revisions on the basis of departmental submissions, taking into account recommendations and decisions of specialized intergovernmental bodies; and

• Provides advice and support to relevant intergovernmental and expert bodies in their review of the programme plan and its revisions; assists in securing approval from the General Assembly.

Budget preparation:

• Reviews, analyses and assists in the finalization of cost estimates and budget proposals, in terms of staff and non-staff requirements from (a) Departments/offices at Headquarters and in the field, including programmatic aspects; (b) smaller-sized peacekeeping operations; ensure compliance with the programme plan and other legislative mandates;

• Audits premium billings and allocates premium costs, monitoring expenses and estimating cost implications due to changes in exposures;

• Assists managers in the elaboration of resource requirements for budget submissions; and

• Provides support to relevant intergovernmental and expert bodies in their budget review and assists in securing approval from the General Assembly.

Budget administration:

• Prepares allotments/appropriations, including redeployment of funds when necessary, ensuring appropriate expenditures;

• Monitors budget implementation and recommends reallocation of funds as necessary;

• Monitors expenditures to ensure that they remain within authorized levels;

• Reviews requisitions for goods and services to ensure (a) correct objects of expenditure have been charged, and (b)availability of funds;

• Administers and monitors extra-budgetary resources, including review of agreements and cost plans, ensuring compliance with regulations and rules and established policies and procedures;

• Assists in the preparation of budget performance submissions;

• Reviews and assists in finalization of budget performance reports, analyzing variances between approved budgets and actual expenditures; and

• Assists in providing substantive support to intergovernmental and expert bodies.

Finance :

• Reviews, approves, reconciles and processes a range of accounting transactions on a regular and recurring basis;

• Audits premium billings and allocates premium costs, monitoring expenses and estimating cost implications due to changes in exposures;

• Reviews and analyses suspense accounts during the year and prepares adjusting entries as required before preparation of financial statements;

• Responsible for the issuance and control of petty cash funds, to ensure compliance with the UN Financial Regulations and Rules;

• Assists with the preparation of cash-flow statements for multiple accounts on a monthly basis;

• Reviews and evaluates financial reports from Offices-away-from Headquarters and Peacekeeping Missions with a view to identifying anomalies and unusual trends. Initiates corrective action;

• Assists in the review and preparation of financial statements and reports;

• Assists in ensuring that accurate and complete accounting, reporting and internal control systems are functioning and that all relevant records are maintained;

• Plans and works with systems units, in the installation and administration of accounting systems; and

• Researches and analyses information needed to respond to audit findings.

General:

• Keeps up-to-date on documents/reports/guidelines that have a bearing on matters related to programme and/or peacekeeping budgets, ensuring compliance with intergovernmental recommendations and decisions as well as with United Nations policies and procedures;

• Keeps up-to-date on current financial regulations/professional publications and accepted principles;

• Drafts memorandum on insurance procurement for approval as appropriate;

• Reviews, analyses and processes insurance claims;

• Undertakes and ensures that correspondence and queries from clients on risk management and commercial insurance matters are appropriately handled; and

• Performs other related duties as assigned.

